# Pinned spark-sdk commit that glow-app's build pipeline expects.
#
# CI checks out the SHA directly. To move glow-app onto a newer
# spark-sdk commit, update the SHA on the last non-comment line and
# commit. scripts/resolve-spark-sdk.sh reads only the first
# non-comment, non-blank line as the SHA. The pinned commit must
# exist on origin (breez/spark-sdk) for CI to check it out.
#
# Pin: main tip (a86bdab9) with the passkey work merged. Reduced passkey
#   API: the CredentialRegistry abstraction is gone (no
#   credentialRegistry / onRegistryError provider options, no
#   PasskeyClient.credentials()), RegisteredCredential is now
#   PasskeyCredential, and register / signIn / connectWithPasskey all
#   return a unified `credential`. Provider config is grouped: rpId /
#   rpName / userName / userDisplayName now live on a
#   PasskeyProviderOptions passed to the PasskeyProvider constructor
#   (and settable on PasskeyConfig for the zero-config client).
#
#   glow-app's capacitor-passkey-prf plugin (Swift + Kotlin) owns its
#   known-credentials store directly (KeychainCredentialRegistry /
#   BlockStoreCredentialRegistry, no longer the SDK's removed
#   CredentialRegistry interface) and records credential IDs after each
#   ceremony; it builds the SDK PasskeyProvider via PasskeyProviderOptions.
#   glow-web's JS passkey layer is migrated in lockstep (submodule bumped
#   to the matching commit).
